# Target TODO

## Remove in 0.25

Everything below exists only to clean up state written by v0.23.x and earlier. Delete it
together. Records without `emitted_json` are the trigger: MCP records lack it through v0.23.x
(OpenCode's from v0.19.0), hook records before v0.12.0.

- `McpFile.legacy` and the adapters' `legacy:` specs (Claude `.claude/.mcp.json`, Codex
  `.codex/codex_mcp.json`, Cursor's same-file legacy), with `Ownership::Legacy`, the legacy
  arm of `mcp_file::reconcile` (the record loop's `file.legacy` lookup, the empty-file delete),
  `Doc::is_empty`, and the MCP half of `has_unrecorded` and the legacy chain in
  `preflight_config_entries`.
- The `Option` on `ConfigEntryRecord.emitted_json`: hook records always serialize and, after
  the above, so do MCP records, so `None` cannot occur.
- The lock v2 promotion (`LockFileV2Wire`, `promote_v2_lock` in `src/lock/`). It was kept for
  the hook sweeps, now removed; v2 locks still promote until it goes.

Also in 0.25: after `mars remove` or `unlink` the MCP file is left as `{}` when the section
empties; delete a file that holds only an empty section, whatever its location.
